{
	title: 'Rate-limited spawns fail; commands keep subagents closing',
	spec: 'spawn refuses, spending no slot, a model rate limited on every account that could run it (auth.limitedUntil): the error names the model, the UTC time it frees up and points to inspect models. inspect models marks each model limited on every account with "(rate limited until <UTC time>)". A human slash command (/model, /pause) to a subagent is not a prompt: only a human prompt or amend promotes it to subagent-leave-open. Invariant restored: a subagent tab closes after its clean finish unless a human sent it a prompt.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Before, prompts.submit promoted before parsing, so /model on a spawned tab silently disabled its auto-close. The regression test must open the child first: a submit to an unopened tab is dropped and the test passed vacuously.',
		'limitedUntil checks the limit key per account for anthropic/openai logins and the account-less key for other providers; with no login it reports free, so the turn reports the login problem.'
